# Normalise line endings in the repository, and check out with LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, Git warns on every add that LF will become CRLF on the next
# checkout, and a Windows contributor ends up committing CRLF while a Linux one
# commits LF — so the same file shows as fully rewritten whenever it crosses
# platforms, and `git blame` stops being useful.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lockfiles are generated; a manual conflict resolution in one is always wrong.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated

# The research notes and the plan document are prose. Marking them keeps GitHub's
# language statistics from counting them as the bulk of the repository.
research/*.md linguist-documentation
*.md linguist-documentation
